# Repository hygiene
.Rproj.user/
.Rhistory
.RData
.Ruserdata
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# Large / regenerated intermediates — never commit these
*.fasta
*.fa
*.faa
*.fna
*.gb
*.gbk
*.aln
*.treefile
*.contree
*.iqtree
*.log
*.ckp
*.bionj
*.mldist
*.model.gz
*.hmm
*.xlsx.tmp

# Cluster / scheduler noise
core.*
slurm-*.out
nohup.out

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Rendered figure output directories (final figure rendering is outside the repository reproducibility scope)
analysis/**/publication_figures_FINAL*/
out/
figs/
# Note the trailing /* — excluding `figures/` outright would also swallow the
# README that explains where the plotting code lives.
figures/*

# Tool metadata leaked by the author's editor
.aipclass
.aipgarb

# Keep these — deliberate exceptions
!supplementary/Data_S1.xlsx
!checksums/SHA256SUMS.txt
!figures/README.md
# Frozen phylogenies are released derived inputs, not regenerated intermediates.
!data/analysis_data/phylogeny/**/*.treefile
# TSWV Fig. 5 inputs: five gene trees + three segment trees + their IQ-TREE
# support files are frozen analysis outputs, the same class as the twelve-family
# trees above. The plotting script reads treefile/contree/iqtree and the codon
# alignments from analysis/06_TSWV_evolution/pipeline_results/.
!analysis/06_TSWV_evolution/pipeline_results/**
# --- R / Python working artefacts
.Rhistory
.RData
.Rproj.user/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# --- Analysis run outputs (regenerated by analysis/*/analysis/*.R)
# NOTE: analysis/<module>/tables/ is NOT disposable — those tables are the exact
# inputs the publication plotting scripts read through TABLE_DIR. They are
# deterministic products of the analysis scripts, so releasing them keeps the
# figure pipeline self-contained (L3 in docs/reproducibility.md). They are
# tracked deliberately.
analysis/*/qc/
analysis/*/logs/
analysis/*/work/
# pipeline_results/ is NOT ignored wholesale: the 12-family QC tables wired into
# pipeline_results/03K_family_specific_markers/ are required inputs for 03L and
# are released. Only the regenerated outputs below are excluded.
analysis/*/pipeline_results/*/tables/
analysis/*/pipeline_results/*/logs/
analysis/*/plot/*/main/
analysis/*/plot/*/panels/
analysis/*/plot/*/supplementary/
analysis/*/plot/*/logs/

# --- Large binaries that are shipped via data/ only
*.mldist
*.ckp.gz
*.splits.nex
*.state
*.rate
*.bionj
*.contree.bak
*.log

# --- Corrections for the released twelve-family phylogeny set
# The blanket *.treefile / *.faa / *.fasta rules above are meant for scratch
# intermediates. The published trees and alignments in data/ and the QC tables
# wired into pipeline_results/ are released derived inputs and must be tracked.
!data/analysis_data/phylogeny/**
!analysis/02_host_relatedness_and_phylogeny/pipeline_results/**
!analysis/02_host_relatedness_and_phylogeny/pipeline_results/03K_family_specific_markers/08_final_12family_trees

# The 03L run directory used to be excluded here as a regenerated output. That was
# wrong: 03L_FINAL_aggregate.R reads the per-family 01_main_summary.tsv,
# 04_pair_sampling_stability_summary.tsv, 05_support_stratified_summary.tsv and
# 07_min_support_sensitivity_summary.tsv, and Fig. 2 reads
# 07_FINAL_plot_ready_family_summary.tsv. Excluding them meant the twelve-family
# block could not be rebuilt from a clone at all. The per-family tables are now
# tracked. What stays out is the byte-level scratch 03L rewrites on every run and
# no downstream script reads: the per-iteration drawings and the tree/alignment
# dumps.
analysis/02_host_relatedness_and_phylogeny/pipeline_results/03L_FINAL_12family_host_spectrum/*/*iteration*.tsv
analysis/02_host_relatedness_and_phylogeny/pipeline_results/03L_FINAL_12family_host_spectrum/*/*.fasta
analysis/02_host_relatedness_and_phylogeny/pipeline_results/03L_FINAL_12family_host_spectrum/*/*.faa
analysis/02_host_relatedness_and_phylogeny/pipeline_results/*/logs/
